    "title": "WWE RAW Sinks To One Of Its Lowest Cagematch Ratings As Fans Slam Show - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Thomas Lowson ,\n53 minutes ago\nThe go-home WWE RAW before SummerSlam 2026 will go down in history, but not for the right reasons, but as one of the most hated episodes of RAW.\nThe show saw the build continue towards SummerSlam, as well as Raquel Rodriguez win the Women’s Intercontinental Title from Sol Ruca.\nREAD MORE: The Undertaker Slams Attitude Era Angle – ‘It Sucked, I Hated It’\nREAD MORE: Chelsea Green Is Dealing With PTSD\nDespite this title change, the show currently has a 2.72 rating on Cagematch , where fans can rate shows, one of the worst ratings for any episode of RAW.\nSeveral reviews highlighted the use of Ryan Garcia, as well as the opening weigh-in segment with Oba Femi and Brock Lesnar that didn’t feature a weigh-in.\nWhile the quality of the matches was seen as fine, the bouts were criticized as ones fans have seen plenty of times before.\nSome said that the feud between the Bloodline and LA Knigh/Solo Sikoa/Royce Keys has an unclear heel-face dynamic, and the title match should’ve been at a pay-per-view event.",
    "summary": "The show saw the build continue towards SummerSlam, as well as Raquel Rodriguez win the Women’s Intercontinental Title from Sol Ruca. READ MORE: The Undertaker Slams Attitude Era Angle – ‘It Sucked, I Hated It’ READ MORE: Chelsea Green Is Dealing With PTSD Despite this title change, the show currently has a 2.72 rating on Cagematch , where fans can rate shows, one of the worst ratings for any episode of RAW. Several reviews highlighted the use of Ryan Garcia, as well as the opening weigh-in segment with Oba Femi and Brock Lesnar that didn’t feature a weigh-in.",
